# Rocdown

Rocdown is the optional document layer on the Rocci stack. Write pages in
Markdown, declare metadata with `@page`, and keep presentation in `.rocci`
layouts. Rust owns the catalog; Rocci owns the visible shell.

This layer is **experimental** — more so than templates. You do not need
Rocdown to ship an application. Static pages are Markdown-first. Live pages
reuse the [application](/docs/applications/) layer: same handlers,
same Datastar transport.

:note[title: "Static pages stay Markdown-first"] {{
    Ordinary `.rocdown` site pages cannot include `@roc` or `@component`
    islands yet. Use article blocks such as `:note` and Markdown here; put
    chrome in a project theme.
}}

